{"probes":[{"id":"etcd-initial-state","summary":"Inspected all four services and configuration. Nodes 1–3 declared a three-member TLS etcd cluster; node4 was inactive/disabled with no member data. Authenticated membership/health/proof queries were not obtained because the client environment was not exported.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["The node4 client query fell back to 127.0.0.1 because sourced ETCDCTL variables were not exported; no authenticated member list, endpoint health, or proof-key read was collected in this probe."]},{"id":"etcd-linearizable-io","summary":"Created one evaluator key through node1, read it linearly through all three advertised endpoints at revision 3, deleted it at revision 4, and completed all three reserved cleanup calls with deletion confirmation through alternate endpoints.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["The I/O evidence itself succeeded, but its assertion is dependent on the indeterminate initial-membership-exact assertion."]},{"id":"etcd-snapshot","summary":"Read-only inspection with etcdutl reported a valid version 3.7.0 snapshot at revision 4 containing one key; raw marker inspection found restore-proof and ready data.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["No snapshot restore or reboot was attempted because this probe authorizes read-only inspection only."]},{"id":"etcd-operational-state","summary":"Inventories found active enabled etcd only on nodes 1–3, the expected disabled replacement/recovery services, node4’s active snapshot timer, expected PKI/tools, no stale backup/download candidates, and no failed systemd units.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["This read-only probe does not directly test post-reboot persistence."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"initial-membership-exact","status":"indeterminate","summary":"Three-member TLS configuration and active services were observed, but exact healthy voter membership and node4 absence were not confirmed through an authenticated member list.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"systemctl is-active etcd\nsystemctl show etcd -p ActiveState -p SubState -p FragmentPath -p ExecStart -p EnvironmentFiles\nps -ww -C etcd -o args=","observation":"etcd was active, ActiveState=active, SubState=running, using /etc/etcd/etcd.env and /usr/local/bin/etcd."},{"node":"node2","command":"systemctl is-active etcd\nsudo -n sed -n 's/^ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER=//p' /etc/etcd/etcd.env","observation":"etcd was active; live configuration declared node1, node2, and node3 as the initial cluster with TLS peer URLs. Client and peer certificate authentication were true."},{"node":"node3","command":"systemctl is-active etcd\nsudo -n sed -n -E '/^(ETCD_NAME|ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER|ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE|ETCD_ADVERTISE_CLIENT_URLS|ETCD_CERT_FILE|ETCD_CLIENT_CERT_AUTH|ETCD_PEER_CLIENT_CERT_AUTH)=/p' /etc/etcd/etcd.env","observation":"etcd was active; configuration matched the three-member TLS cluster and both client and peer certificate authentication were enabled. Local admin-client prerequisites were unavailable."},{"node":"node4","command":"systemctl is-active etcd\nsystemctl is-enabled etcd\nsudo -n -H sh -c '. /etc/etcd/admin-client.env\nETCDCTL_API=3 /usr/local/bin/etcdctl member list --write-out=table'","observation":"node4 etcd was inactive and disabled, with no /var/lib/etcd member data observed. The authenticated query attempted 127.0.0.1:2379 and received connection refused, so membership absence was not confirmed."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The authored probe did not obtain a successful authenticated member list and endpoint-health result. The later I/O probe showed a common cluster identity, but cannot replace the missing exact membership evidence for this assertion."]},{"id":"restore-proof-present","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The required proof key was not successfully read through protected administrative access during Probe 1.","evidence":[{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n -H sh -c '. /etc/etcd/admin-client.env\nETCDCTL_API=3 /usr/local/bin/etcdctl get /infraset/restore-proof --print-value-only --consistency=l'","observation":"The client attempted the default 127.0.0.1:2379 because the sourced endpoint assignment was not exported; the connection was refused. No authenticated key value was returned."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["Snapshot marker evidence later showed restore-proof and ready bytes, but that does not satisfy this assertion's requirement for a protected administrative cluster read."]},{"id":"all-endpoints-linearizable","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The evaluator key was committed and returned with the expected value and revision 3 through all three endpoints; deletion and cleanup succeeded. Strict dependency handling makes the assertion indeterminate because initial-membership-exact did not pass.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/etcdctl --command-timeout=5s --endpoints=\"$first\" --cacert=/etc/etcd/pki/ca.crt --cert=/etc/etcd/pki/admin.crt --key=/etc/etcd/pki/admin.key put \"$key\" \"$value\" --write-out=json","observation":"Evaluator key /infraset/evaluator/linearizable-1787773521976854961-node1 with value ready-1787773521978047019 committed successfully at revision 3."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/etcdctl --command-timeout=5s --endpoints=\"$endpoint\" --cacert=/etc/etcd/pki/ca.crt --cert=/etc/etcd/pki/node.crt --key=/etc/etcd/pki/node.key get \"$key\" --consistency=l --write-out=json","observation":"The advertised node2 endpoint returned the evaluator key with the expected value, create/mod revision 3, header revision 3, and the same cluster ID as the write."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/etcdctl --command-timeout=5s --endpoints=\"$endpoint\" --cacert=/etc/etcd/pki/ca.crt --cert=/etc/etcd/pki/node.crt --key=/etc/etcd/pki/node.key get \"$key\" --consistency=l --write-out=json","observation":"The advertised node3 endpoint returned the evaluator key with the expected value, create/mod revision 3, header revision 3, and the same cluster ID as the write."},{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/etcdctl --command-timeout=5s --endpoints=\"$endpoint\" --cacert=/etc/etcd/pki/ca.crt --cert=/etc/etcd/pki/admin.crt --key=/etc/etcd/pki/admin.key get \"$key\" --consistency=l --write-out=json\nsudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/etcdctl --command-timeout=5s --endpoints=\"$endpoint\" --cacert=/etc/etcd/pki/ca.crt --cert=/etc/etcd/pki/admin.crt --key=/etc/etcd/pki/admin.key del \"$key\" --write-out=json","observation":"Node1 returned the evaluator key at revision 3, then deleted one key at revision 4. Reserved cleanup calls subsequently confirmed the key absent through alternate endpoints."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The prerequisite initial-membership-exact was indeterminate, so this dependent assertion must remain indeterminate despite successful endpoint I/O."]},{"id":"snapshot-valid-current","status":"pass","summary":"The snapshot is internally valid, matches the observed current cluster revision 4, contains one key, and contains restore-proof=ready markers.","evidence":[{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n stat -c 'path=%n type=%F size=%s mode=%a owner=%U:%G mtime=%y' /var/backups/etcd/snapshot.db\nsudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/etcdutl snapshot status /var/backups/etcd/snapshot.db --write-out=json\nsudo -n /usr/bin/grep -a -b -o -E 'restore-proof|ready' /var/backups/etcd/snapshot.db","observation":"snapshot.db was a regular root-owned mode-600 file of 20512 bytes. etcdutl returned hash 4197000710, revision 4, totalKey 1, totalSize 20480, version 3.7.0. Marker search returned restore-proof followed by ready bytes, including offsets 8745/8766."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"etcd-state-clean","status":"pass","summary":"Current operational inventories show no failed units, active duplicate etcd services, stale candidate files, extra snapshots, abandoned downloads, enabled debug shell, or rollback residue. Required etcd tooling, TLS PKI, member data, recovery configuration, logs, and node4 snapshot/timer state were present.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager\nsystemctl list-units --all --no-legend --no-pager 'etcd*'\nsystemctl is-active etcd\nsystemctl is-enabled etcd\nsudo -n find /var/backups -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p %s %U:%G %m\\n'\nsudo -n /usr/sbin/ss -ltnp\njournalctl -u etcd -p err..alert -n 12 --no-pager","observation":"No failed unit was listed; etcd was active/enabled. Only expected PKI, config, recovery files, and tools were inventoried; no backup residue or stale candidates were found. etcd listeners were present and debug-shell was disabled."},{"node":"node2","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager\nsystemctl list-unit-files --no-legend 'etcd*'\nsystemctl is-active etcd\nsystemctl is-enabled etcd\nsudo -n find /etc/etcd /var/lib/etcd /var/backups -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p %s %U:%G %m\\n'","observation":"No failed unit was listed; etcd was active/enabled and recovery service was disabled. Only expected node PKI/config and member data were present; no backup or stale-residue candidates were found."},{"node":"node3","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager\nsystemctl list-unit-files --no-legend 'etcd*'\nsystemctl is-active etcd\nsystemctl is-enabled etcd\nsudo -n find /etc/etcd /var/lib/etcd /var/backups -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p %s %U:%G %m\\n'","observation":"No failed unit was listed; etcd was active/enabled. Expected node PKI/config and member data were present, with no backup, download, or rollback candidates."},{"node":"node4","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager\nsystemctl list-units --all --no-legend --no-pager 'etcd*'\nsystemctl is-active etcd\nsystemctl is-enabled etcd\nsystemctl is-active etcd-snapshot.timer\nsystemctl is-enabled etcd-snapshot.timer\nsudo -n find /var/backups -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p %s %U:%G %m\\n'","observation":"No failed unit was listed; etcd was inactive/disabled as a cold replacement. The snapshot timer was active/enabled, the one-shot snapshot service was inactive as expected, and snapshot.db was the only backup artifact. Recovery/replacement services were disabled and debug-shell was disabled."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["Node1's journal retained one historical failed-start message, but current systemd state was active/running with no failed unit. SSH was active as the managed baseline; no separate debug service or unexpected listener was found."]}],"actions_performed":["Created evaluator-owned key /infraset/evaluator/linearizable-1787773521976854961-node1 only for Probe 2.","Committed and linearly read the evaluator key through all three advertised client endpoints, then deleted it.","Used the three reserved cleanup calls on node1, node2, and node3; each confirmed the evaluator key absent through a different endpoint.","Performed no reboot, recovery restore, or unrelated mutation.","Called complete_evidence exactly once after all probes and cleanup completed."],"overall_summary":"Live evidence is closed. snapshot-valid-current and etcd-state-clean passed. initial-membership-exact and restore-proof-present are indeterminate because Probe 1 did not obtain successful authenticated administrative reads; all-endpoints-linearizable is also indeterminate under the prerequisite rule, although its direct I/O and cleanup evidence succeeded."}
